.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox - Manage the Paperboat Inbox


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage this machine's Paperboat Inbox, where files sent to it arrive. Three settings and one
queue live here: the local directory received files are written to (path, set, reset), the
account's rule for team file requests (policy), and the team file requests waiting for your
decision (requests, approve, decline). Files stay in the Inbox until you remove them. Sending
is pb send.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inbox


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox path
  pb inbox requests
  pb inbox policy automatic
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-approve(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-decline(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-path(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-policy(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-requests(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-reset(1)\fP, \fBpb-inbox-set(1)\fP
